## Implementation Agent re-prompt template (for Validation Agent output)

When validation fails, the Validation Agent must produce a prompt in a \`\`\`text\`\`\`
block that the user can paste into a new Implementation Agent session. Include this
template in the plan so the Planner and Validation Agent know the format:

\```text
You are Implementation Agent <A/B/...> for <plan name>.

Validation Agent has completed a read-only validation pass. The following defects
were found that you must fix.

DEFECT 1
File: <path>
<What is wrong. What the fix should be.>

DEFECT 2
File: <path>
<What is wrong. What the fix should be.>

REQUIRED FIX
1. <First action>
2. <Second action>

Read the plan file and rules before making changes. Do not run deploy.py or copy
files to X:\. Run the full test suite after your changes and confirm it passes:
  <test suite command>
\```
```

---

### Common pitfalls

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
|---------|-------|-----|
| Implementation Agent ignores half the requirements | Detail was in chat, not the plan file | Move ALL detail into the plan file before producing prompts |
| Validation Agent gives a vague "PASS" without checking | Checklist not specific enough | Each checklist item must be verifiable by reading one file/method |
| Parallel agents conflict on the same file | Parallelism analysis missing or wrong | Map every file to exactly one track; shared files go in one track |
| Validation Agent modifies code | Prompt didn't say read-only | Always include "DO NOT modify any files" in the Validation prompt |
| Agent uses wrong rule files | Prompt didn't list them | Always list `@` rule references explicitly in every prompt |
| Fresh agent re-explores the whole codebase | Plan lacked context | Include file paths, line numbers, and architecture diagram |
| Agent tries to deploy to production | Not stated in prompt | Always include "DO NOT run deploy.py" |
| Implementation Agent skips the test suite | Test command not in prompt | Always include the exact test command with WSL path |
| User doesn't know what order to run agents | Plan doesn't explain the dependency | Parallelism analysis must clearly state which tracks can run simultaneously and which must be sequential |
| Validation re-prompt is hard to act on | FAIL output is vague or not copy-pasteable | Validation Agent must produce a fenced \`\`\`text\`\`\` block with a complete Implementation Agent prompt: defects (file + defect + fix), required actions, test command, no-deploy constraint |
| Prompts reference placeholders instead of the real plan path | Planner forgot to replace `{{PLAN_PATH}}` after creating the plan | Update the generated plan so every prompt contains the concrete `C:\Users\thaynes\.cursor\plans\...` path |
| Validation says PASS but important issues remain | No final planner review happened | After implementation/validation are complete, the original Planner Agent should re-run tests and do a code-review/fix pass |

---

### After creating a plan (Planner checklist)

- [ ] Plan file path is correct and the file was created successfully
- [ ] Every todo has a clear owner track in the parallelism analysis
- [ ] No file appears in more than one track (unless read-only access)
- [ ] Both prompts are in fenced `text` code blocks (easy copy-paste)
- [ ] Both prompts reference the exact plan file path
- [ ] Both prompts list the relevant `@` rule files
- [ ] Both prompts include the test suite command
- [ ] Both prompts include the no-deploy constraint
- [ ] Validation prompt says "DO NOT modify any files"
- [ ] Validation prompt instructs Validation Agent to produce a copy-pasteable Implementation Agent re-prompt when FAIL (see Implementation Agent re-prompt template)
- [ ] Validation checklist covers every requirement — not just happy path, also logging, backward compat, edge cases
- [ ] For parallel splits: prompts clearly state which todos each agent owns
- [ ] Prompts reference the concrete created plan path, not a placeholder
- [ ] Plan includes the final planner review step after implementation/validation
